Alembic migrations for ap-agent.

The database URL is read from settings in env.py, not from alembic.ini.

  just db-up        start Postgres
  just db-revision "add x"   autogenerate a revision from the models
  just db-migrate   upgrade to head

Two roles, not one:

  ap_agent      owns the schema and runs migrations (database_migration_url)
  ap_agent_app  serves traffic                      (database_url)

The split is load-bearing rather than tidy. Revision 0002 revokes UPDATE,
DELETE and TRUNCATE on audit_events, and a revoke only binds against a role that
is subject to grants - a superuser bypasses the check entirely, which is exactly
what made the same revoke in 0001 a no-op.

Provisioning creates roles; migrations grant privileges. Locally the role comes
from docker/initdb/010-app-role.sql. In production it comes from your
infrastructure, and 0002 grants to whatever AP_AGENT_DB_APP_ROLE names.

Verify it after any change to the audit schema:

  psql -U ap_agent_app -d ap_agent -c "UPDATE audit_events SET decision='x';"
  # must print: ERROR: permission denied for table audit_events
